@startuml
' Simplified overview by Vincent Lin with OpenAI Codex assistance.
' Based on ArchitectureSequenceDiagram.puml, including Ernest Chua's command-flow work.
' This diagram groups internal calls; labels describe responsibilities, not Java method signatures.

title Editing a person: save before showing success
hide footbox
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 17
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequenceParticipantPadding 24
skinparam sequenceBoxPadding 12
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #374151
  LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupHeaderFontColor #334155
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

participant "Session" as Session #EDE9FE
participant "Command executor" as Executor #DBEAFE
participant "File writer" as Writer #FEF3C7

[-> Session : edit 1 n/Jamie Tan
Session -> Executor : Run the validated command
Executor -> Executor : Prepare the edit\non a separate copy

note over Executor
  Live records have not changed.
end note

Executor -> Writer : Save the complete snapshot

alt Save succeeds
  Writer --> Executor : Saved
  Executor -> Executor : Apply the saved change\nand refresh the views
  Executor --> Session : Success
  [<-- Session : Show success feedback
else Save fails
  Writer --> Executor : Save error
  Executor --> Session : Failure; live data unchanged
  [<-- Session : Show failure feedback
end

caption Example: valid input that changes a person's details.\nInvalid input and unchanged edits are outside this overview.
@enduml
